   "text": "I read the molecule region by region and wrote it as a SMILES. It looks like a PROTAC-type molecule that joins a VHL-ligand end to an aminopyridazine\u2013phenol end.\n\n**Left end (aminopyridazine\u2013phenol):**\n- A pyridazine carries NH2, a 2-hydroxyphenyl group, and a ring nitrogen of a 3,8-diazabicyclo[3.2.1]octane.\n- The bridging N8 of that bicycle is bonded to the C2 of a pyrimidine.\n\n**Linker:**\n- The pyrimidine C5 carries an alkyne, then three CH2 groups, then N-methyl.\n- That nitrogen is attached to a cyclohexane ring at the 1,4-positions. The cyclohexane has no stereochemistry drawn, so I left it unspecified.\n\n**Right end (VHL ligand):**\n- The other cyclohexane carbon bears an alpha carbon with an NH\u2013C(=O)\u2013(1-fluorocyclopropyl) amide and a C(=O) bonded to the pyrrolidine nitrogen.\n- The pyrrolidine has a 4-hydroxy group and a 2-carboxamide.\n- The amide nitrogen is bonded to a benzyl group whose para position carries a 4-methylthiazol-5-yl group.\n\n**Stereochemistry:** I assigned the hydroxyproline and the alpha carbon by analogy with the standard VH032 pattern (2S,4R proline, S alpha carbon), rather than deriving them independently from the drawn wedges. Since the cyclohexyl group ranks the same as tert-butyl at that centre, the same chirality tags apply.\n\nSMILES: Nc1nnc(-c2ccccc2O)cc1N1CC2CCC(C1)N2c1ncc(C#CCCCN(C)C2CCC(CC2)[C@H](NC(=O)C2(F)CC2)C(=O)N2C[C@H](O)C[C@H]2C(=O)NCc2ccc(cc2)-c2scnc2C)cn1"
